msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:91
#: 2b1eb225f4e34df8a22279bcd76b1e67
msgid ""
"The unpruned Cartesian product yields $3 \\\\times 5 \\\\times 2 = 30$ "
"permutations per Python interpreter (150 combinations across all 5 "
"supported Python versions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:94
#: c218032a68e640d8bf7adce32cf45ceb
msgid "3.2. Pruning `--prerelease` Permutations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:96
#: 0bd816e809304a0985868fee92af2cdc
msgid ""
"Inspecting `[project].dependencies` and `[dependency-groups].test` in "
"`pyproject.toml` shows that every dependency specifier uses a stable "
"lower bound (`>=X.Y` or `>=X.Y.Z`) with zero explicit pre-release "
"specifiers (such as `>=1.0a1` or `>=2.0.0rc1`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:100
#: a133bd3351a141498ef2de91c7c3f872
msgid ""
"**Eliminate `explicit` and `if-necessary-or-explicit` (-12 "
"combinations)**: Because no specifier in `pyproject.toml` opts into an "
"explicit pre-release tag, `--prerelease explicit` is mathematically "
"identical to `--prerelease disallow`, and `--prerelease if-necessary-or-"
"explicit` is identical to `--prerelease if-necessary` across all "
"resolutions and fork strategies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:104
#: 39388948b32c424bab762ad2ba491f11
msgid ""
"**Eliminate `if-necessary` under `highest` and `lowest-direct` (-4 "
"combinations)**: Every direct and transitive dependency of `findfmt` has "
"published stable wheels satisfying `>=3.11`. Under `highest` and `lowest-"
"direct`, the solver never lacks a stable candidate, so `if-necessary` "
"produces the exact same resolution graph as `disallow`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:108
#: b295523ae77946e5929b54e9c45a3f98
msgid ""
"**Retain `(lowest, if-necessary, fewest)` and eliminate `(lowest, "
"disallow, *)` / `(lowest, allow, *)` (-5 combinations)**: Full transitive"
" `--resolution lowest` attempts to pick the oldest historical release of "
"every transitive package (`click`, `pygments`, `markdown-it-py`, `mdurl`,"
" `packaging`). Using `if-necessary` allows the solver to fall back only "
"when an ancient transitive sdist lacks metadata, whereas `lowest` + "
"`allow` selects broken historical alpha tags from transitive dependencies"
" that are unrelated to `findfmt`'s own version bounds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:115
#: 53d337375f6d4c159cdb14579d289a11
msgid "3.3. Pruning `--fork-strategy` Permutations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:117
#: 8d569a3f9427446fb6fc92e5df0de965
msgid ""
"`uv`'s `--fork-strategy` flag (`fewest` versus `requires-python`) "
"controls how the universal resolver splits resolution forks across "
"disjoint Python version ranges:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:120
#: 71adc20b1ba3430c815b42ccbb3dfaf5
msgid ""
"When resolving into a single target interpreter environment (`uv pip "
"install --python <env>`), environment markers (`python_version < '3.12'` "
"for `typing-extensions>=4`) evaluate to a fixed boolean for that "
"interpreter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:123
#: 10fc2f9472734f9c97e07140f5df9ca0
msgid ""
"Consequently, varying `--fork-strategy` across all `lowest-direct` and "
"`allow` permutations produces identical per-interpreter package sets (-8 "
"combinations)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:125
#: e764d96bc1b943d8bd24093391570560
msgid ""
"Retaining a single `(highest, disallow, requires-python)` cell verifies "
"that `--fork-strategy requires-python` succeeds cleanly against "
"`findfmt`'s `requires-python = \">=3.11\"` metadata."
msgstr ""

