#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:145
#: 16a48c5a24834922bbaeb2042a87f98b
msgid "4. Failure Diagnostic Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:147
#: f2cabbb3ec404c6fb6fca784d57a8afc
msgid ""
"When any resolution or `pytest` step fails in CI or local matrix "
"execution, the runner executes a three-stage diagnostic pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:150
#: eece47633cc14e7598a68744df23fdbf
msgid "4.1. Stage 1 — Ephemeral Dependency Tree Capture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:152
#: 7af6afcf936543f5b1ce3fb7468c5808
msgid ""
"Immediately upon resolution or test failure (`if: failure()` in GitHub "
"Actions or non-zero exit code in `tools/verify_quality.py`), the runner "
"captures the resolved dependency graph from the isolated environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:160
#: 7e697548b06a433d810f9544c01683f2
msgid ""
"In GitHub Actions, this output is appended as a fenced Markdown block to "
"`$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY` under the failing cell heading (`### Dependency "
"Tree (<resolution> / <prerelease> / <fork-strategy>)`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:164
#: 04ea0bf51a4c4dfcbd2ac29484e486ed
msgid "4.2. Stage 2 — Baseline Lockfile Version Diffing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:166
#: a67367a3089f468faf85e2114cf2cff1
msgid ""
"To isolate which package version triggered the regression, the runner "
"compares the failing environment's installed package list (`uv pip list "
"--format json --python <env_path>`) against the pinned versions in "
"`uv.lock`, reporting a concise delta table of downgraded or pre-release "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:170
#: 1c806d02c01e48a59ace46060d4bd231
msgid "4.3. Stage 3 — Offending Bound Pinpointing & Remediation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:172
#: fac3d351b716434f92271aedf6537db8
msgid ""
"The diagnostic reporter cross-references installed direct package "
"versions against the specifiers in `pyproject.toml` "
"(`[project].dependencies` and `[dependency-groups].test`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:175
#: 4ae61329597f4d46957b6108f96a7f5d
msgid ""
"If a failure occurs under `lowest-direct` (`M1` or `M4`), the report "
"identifies the direct dependencies pinned at their floor versions and "
"outputs the exact `pyproject.toml` lower bound that requires bumping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/quality/dependency_matrix.md:178
#: 90fcdef35b5b43df84b25db5b909ed07
msgid ""
"If a failure occurs under `prerelease=allow` (`M2` or `M4`), the report "
"highlights every installed package whose version matches a pre-release "
"segment (`a`, `b`, `rc`, `dev`) so maintainers can file upstream reports "
"or add temporary upper-bound exclusions."
msgstr ""
